# Adaptive Thresholding – Practical Implementation

## 1. Input Image

The input is a handwritten image with uneven illumination, loaded in grayscale.

## 2. Adaptive Mean Thresholding

![Adaptive Mean Thresholding](adaptive_mean_output.png)

**Observation:** The local mean intensity is used to calculate the threshold for each pixel.

## 3. Adaptive Gaussian Thresholding

![Adaptive Gaussian Thresholding](adaptive_gaussian_output.png)

**Observation:** A weighted average of neighbouring pixels is used to calculate the local threshold.

## 4. Comparison

Both methods adapt to local lighting conditions. Adaptive Mean uses an ordinary local average, whereas Adaptive Gaussian gives more weight to nearby pixels.

## 5. Result

Both adaptive thresholding techniques were successfully applied to the handwritten image to improve foreground and background separation.
